.TH GREDIST 1 "2026-09-05" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
gredist \- Protocol 47/GRE distributor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gredist
[\fB--syslog\fR] \fIservice_name\fR
.br
.B gredist
.B -c
\fIconfig_path\fR [\fB--syslog\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-gredist
is a small userspace control service that distributes raw Protocol 47/GRE traffic from a single frontend address to a pool of backends. Userspace owns configuration, membership, health and HRW distribution; the kernel handles packet I/O via raw sockets and builds the outer IP header on send. There is no nft fast path.
.PP
Each service is named by its config file:
.B /etc/saphira/gredist/\fIservice_name\fR.conf
and started as
.B gredist \fIservice_name\fR.
.PP
Config is deliberately simple: one
.B frontend=IP
and one or more
.B backend=IP
lines. IPv4 and IPv6 use same syntax; mixed pools and cross-family forwarding (v4->v6, v6->v4) are supported by rebuilding the outer IP envelope while preserving GRE header and inner payload.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.nf
frontend=217.155.241.55
backend=172.16.10.10
backend=172.16.10.11

frontend=2a02:8012:bc57::47
backend=2a02:8012:bc57:100::10
.fi
.PP
Comments start with \fB#\fR or \fB;\fR. Exactly one frontend, at least one backend. Families are not tied.
.SH GRE HANDLING
Parsing follows Linux \fBnet/ipv4/gre_demux.c:gre_parse_header\fR: validate outer IP, check \fBGRE_VERSION\fR and \fBGRE_ROUTING\fR, compute \fBgre_calc_hlen\fR from CSUM/KEY/SEQ, fail closed on truncated or malformed, support keyless and keyed (key is visible tunnel identifier). Fragments (IPv4 frag_off, IPv6 next header 44), oversized (>9000) and queue pressure are counted as drops. An IPv6 packet carrying extension headers before GRE is not parsed and is counted as malformed.
.SH DISTRIBUTION
Rendezvous/HRW hashing on outer source address plus GRE key when present. Score = splitmix64(fnv1a(backend) XOR flow_hash), which depends on the backend's identity and the flow and not on its position in the config. Removal moves only affected flows; reordering the config moves none; rejoin is deterministic.
.SH HEALTH
ICMP ping per backend every 2s; 2 consecutive fails -> down, 2 successes -> up. Logs transitions. No healthy backend -> drop. Probes run as detached children and are reaped by the event loop, so an unresponsive peer does not stall forwarding.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGHUP
reload config,
.B SIGUSR1
dump stats,
.B SIGINT/SIGTERM
exit.
.SH FILES
.B /etc/saphira/gredist/*.conf
.br
.B /var/run/saphira/gredist/
.SH COUNTERS
Counters are in memory only and reset on restart. \fBSIGUSR1\fR reports rx, forwarded and the drops: malformed, truncated, frag, vers, no_backend, queue, oversized, not_for_us. Every accepted packet is accounted for in exactly one of them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B ip-gre(8)
